From: Jetha Chan <jetha@splatterfacegames.com>
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/v4l2_m2m_dec: don't drop a pending packet while the capture queue is not set up

v4l2_receive_frame() keeps a packet in s->buf_pkt when the OUTPUT queue
is full (enqueue returns EAGAIN). It then calls v4l2_try_start(), which
fails while VIDIOC_G_FMT(CAPTURE) is refused because the decoder has not
yet parsed the stream headers, and the error path unrefs s->buf_pkt: the
packet is lost.

On Qualcomm Venus (MSM8953) the firmware may take more than the 16 OUTPUT
buffers before it raises the source change, so packets 16 onwards were
dropped: 2 to 7 frames missing at the start of 1080p H.264 streams, and
with a P-only stream every following frame corrupt until the next IDR.

Wait instead, while a packet is held and CAPTURE is not streaming: retry
v4l2_try_start() and poll through ff_v4l2_context_dequeue_frame(), which
handles the source change event, until the packet can be queued or the
CAPTURE queue is up (bounded at about 5 s). Returning EAGAIN instead is not
an option: the packet stays held, avcodec_send_packet() then returns EAGAIN
and the ffmpeg CLI aborts ("A decoder returned an unexpected error code").
---
diff --git a/libavcodec/v4l2_m2m_dec.c b/libavcodec/v4l2_m2m_dec.c
index ba1fe76..f7c8956 100644
--- a/libavcodec/v4l2_m2m_dec.c
+++ b/libavcodec/v4l2_m2m_dec.c
@@ -154,6 +154,26 @@ static int v4l2_receive_frame(AVCodecContext *avctx, AVFrame *frame)
         goto dequeue;
 
     ret = ff_v4l2_context_enqueue_packet(output, &s->buf_pkt);
+    if (ret == AVERROR(EAGAIN) && !capture->streamon) {
+        /*
+         * All OUTPUT buffers are queued and the CAPTURE queue cannot be set
+         * up until the driver has parsed the headers and signalled a source
+         * change. Wait here for that event (handled by the dequeue below)
+         * or a free OUTPUT buffer instead of returning: v4l2_try_start()
+         * would fail and the packet held in s->buf_pkt would be dropped.
+         */
+        for (int i = 0; i < 50 && ret == AVERROR(EAGAIN) && !capture->streamon; i++) {
+            int r = v4l2_try_start(avctx);
+            if (r == AVERROR(ENOMEM))
+                goto fail;
+            if (!r && capture->streamon)
+                break;
+            r = ff_v4l2_context_dequeue_frame(capture, frame, 100);
+            if (!r)
+                return 0;
+            ret = ff_v4l2_context_enqueue_packet(output, &s->buf_pkt);
+        }
+    }
     if (ret < 0 && ret != AVERROR(EAGAIN))
         goto fail;
 
